WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  this friday marks four years since the  one october massacre 58 people died that  night in 2017 when a gunman opened fire  on the route 91 harvest festival from  mandalay bay friday morning on october  1st the sunrise remembrance ceremony  returns to the clark county government  center downtown then at the evening  friday evening names of the victims will  be read at the downtown healing garden  survivors will also gather at the site  of the shooting to form that route 91  human chain again these are things that  have been done for the last several  years  clark county has also done this once  again they've set up a memorial exhibit  in the rotunda gallery on the first  floor of the clark county government  center this display includes handmade  quilts and the art of healing murals  created by local artists if you're  interested in checking that out you can  stop by and see it through next thursday  the vegas strong 5k and one mile race  also is back this year after taking a  year off for the pandemic it is sunday  morning at floyd lamb park i have the  honor of hosting the event this year  registration for the race though is  closed but if you are taking part a  reminder pick up your packet on friday  from noon until 6 outside of the rei out  at boca park  this week eight news now will have  coverage to commemorate one october  friday morning we're going to share  stories from survivors and talk about  how the city has changed since that  tragic evening we'll also be live during  good day las vegas at the sunrise  service and you can find plenty of  stories on air and online regarding one  october at eight newsnow dot com

